{
  "_README": "Steam Frame override for UEVR. Copy to %APPDATA%\\UnrealVRMod\\SystemReShock-Win64-Shipping\\ (per game) or %APPDATA%\\UnrealVRMod\\UEVR\\Profiles\\ (global). The filename is the interaction profile path /interaction_profiles/valve/frame_controller_valve with slashes turned into underscores. This is the full binding set. A second xrSuggestInteractionProfileBindings call for the same profile replaces the previous bindings, so this set becomes the profile's bindings: the squeeze becomes UEVR's grip (Xbox LB/RB, the grab), and the bumper no longer maps to the shoulder. The bumpers no longer map to the shoulder; they are routed to the free D-pad Up (left) and D-pad Down (right) inputs, which the game leaves unused during gameplay. The plugin reads those two Xbox D-pad bits and treats both bumpers as the action (interact) button. Every path must be valid for the Frame profile or the whole call is rejected and UEVR keeps its native bindings. Action names are the lowercased UEVR manifest names.",
